        explanation: "Maurizio Seracini, a Florence-born engineer and Leonardo specialist, spent decades arguing that Vasari may have built a false wall in front of Leonardo's deteriorating mural rather than destroy it — partly because Vasari left a tiny inscription, 'Cerca, trova' ('Seek, find'), on a banner in his own fresco. In 2012, Seracini was permitted to drill small holes through the Vasari fresco and probe with cameras and chemical samplers. He recovered traces of a black pigment and red lake consistent with Leonardo's known palette, but the work was suspended amid protest from preservationists who feared damage to the Vasari. The question remains open.",
